## Important Formula

Profit Share ∝ Investment × Time

So,

A's Share : B's Share = (Investment of A × Time) : (Investment of B × Time)

## Example

A invests ₹10,000 for 12 months and B invests ₹15,000 for 8 months.

A's investment ratio = 10,000 × 12 = 1,20,000

B's investment ratio = 15,000 × 8 = 1,20,000

Therefore,

A : B = 1 : 1

So, both will get an equal share of profit.

## Key Learning

In partnership problems, profit is divided according to the **ratio of investment and time**.

